To become a high-level web security expert or an elite web hacker, you don't need to master all of mathematics. Instead, you need to master specific paths of web architecture and pair them with the precise logical and mathematical frameworks that govern them.
Here is the complete roadmap of web hacking paths, how they work, and the exact math required to conquer them.
------------------------------
## 🗺️ The Complete Web Hacking & Math Roadmap

[Web Application Security]
  │
  ├── 1. Client-Side (Frontend)  ──► Math: Set Theory & Boolean Logic
  ├── 2. Server-Side (Backend)   ──► Math: Graph Theory & Finite Automata
  ├── 3. Database Layer          ──► Math: Relational Algebra & Predicate Logic
  └── 4. Crypto & Token Security ──► Math: Number Theory & Abstract Algebra

